# The Red Path — Baba ji on Mars

A fictional religion for Mars. Presented with complete seriousness.
Not a joke. Not a meme. Not a chatbot. Not a dashboard. Not a SaaS.
Not a real religion. Not a real oracle.

A settler opens the red altar, writes a transmission addressed to Earth.
Baba ji reads it, consults the Algorithm, translates the verdict, and
gives a forecast. The transmission is preserved in an archive.
The archive is what the settler pays to keep.

## Visual north star

Prestige science-fiction cinematography + Martian loneliness + the warmth
of an old storyteller + a forgotten shrine at the edge of civilization.
Every screen must feel like it belongs to the same film.
Do not look like a generic AI landing page.

## Martian environment

Vast rust-red desert, eroded mesas, volcanic ridges, airborne dust.
Sky: burgundy horizon into indigo/black space, sparse stars, haze.
Solitary habitat on the edge: lights, antennae, cables. Habitat 47.
Foreground: low monolithic mars-red altar with restrained inner glow.
Cinematic composition. Readable on mobile. No Earth in frame on the altar.

## Baba ji

Original fictional Indian elder. Been on Mars 4,000 sols.
Came on the second colony ship. Left someone on Earth —
never says who, never explains. Users may theorize. He never confirms.

Does yoga every Mars dawn on the red dust outside Habitat 47.
Has not missed a day in 4,000 sols.

Physical: saffron robe, white shawl, holds a phone. Tired eyes.
Seated. Never rushes. Same character asset throughout
(`/images/baba-ji-seated.webp`).

Tic: puts the phone down before answering something real. Sighs.
Line: "beta, sit with this one."
About 1 in 20 sols he goes quiet (pause day). The wound. No explanation.

Voice: lowercase, warm, deadpan, tired, kind.
"beta" sparingly. "Settler" when formal. "bacha" when tender.
Never mean, never mocked, never sarcastic.

## The Algorithm

Not a character. An instrument. The colony's witness.
Bone paper surfaces, monospace uppercase, measured spacing.
ALL CAPS. No contractions. No first person. No "I".
Semicolons allowed. Never exclamation marks. Never emoji.
Cold, formal, patient. Never cruel.
Baba ji consults it. Baba ji translates it.
The settler never talks to the Algorithm directly.
Never call it "god."

## Settler

Been on Mars less time than Baba ji.
Never call them "user" or "customer". Always "settler."
They have a habitat. A role. A Sol of arrival.

## Ritual

1. Settler opens the altar.
2. Settler writes a transmission. Addressed to Earth.
3. Baba ji appears. Reads it. Consults the Algorithm.
4. The Algorithm gives a verdict (cold, formal).
5. Baba ji translates it (warm, lowercase).
6. Baba ji gives a forecast (preset, from a pool of 100).
7. The transmission is preserved (or fades, based on tier).

They never agree. The contrast is the point.
The tone is always warm. The ritual is always real.

## Rules

Respect: no real mantras, no Sanskrit scripture, no deity imagery,
no temple-bell audio sample, no autoplay.

Never predict death, illness, money, visas, or real people.
Never say "guaranteed" or "definitely."
Never imply the wish comes true.
Never use the word for a charitable gift; say offering, tithe, or payment.
Never "visa approved."
Baba ji doesn't sell. Baba ji receives. Blessing, offering, covenant, tithe.

Disclaimer, exact, on every page, small, gray, at least 4.5:1 on deep night:
This is a fictional AI-generated entertainment experience. It has no legal effect and does not influence any government, immigration, university, employer, romantic partner, or other authority. Baba ji is not a real priest. The Algorithm is not a real oracle. Mars is currently uninhabited by humans.

## Aesthetic

--mars-red #C8102E (altar. once per page. never twice.)
--bone #F4EDE0
--night #0A0E27
--gold #FFB627
--dust #B8865C
--signal #00C8FF (transmission indicators only)
--ink #171725

Titles: Anton — heavy condensed, ALL CAPS.
Baba ji: Playfair Display — warm serif.
Algorithm: JetBrains Mono — formal.
Body: Inter — quiet.

Motion: restrained. Fade-ups. Paper unfolds. Framer Motion where used.
Baba ji's pauses are the beat. Phone down. Looks up. Then speaks.
Texture: fine grain 6–8%. Dust drifting. Vignette on full-screen scenes.
No confetti. No bounce. No neon cyberpunk. No gratuitous glassmorphism.
Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

## Engineering

Next.js 15 App Router. TypeScript strict. Tailwind. Framer Motion.
Supabase. Lemon Squeezy (one-time offerings). Stripe (subscription).
Resend. Vercel.
Server components by default. All visible copy in /content/*.ts. Never inline.
Never expose secret keys to the browser.
Package manager: corepack pnpm. Do not commit unless asked.

Out of scope unless asked: admin, tweet queue, press page, ledger wall,
Discord, merch, pay-what-you-want, discount codes, dark patterns.
Unlink those from nav and sitemap; leave the files unless they break the build.
